# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — secrets never enter source control, but the template does
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Operational scripts that act directly on a LIVE database, kept out of the
# repository on purpose.
#
# Everything else under scripts/ calls assertNotProduction and refuses to run
# against the real park. These two are the deliberate exceptions — one wipes
# trading data, the other mints an administrator — so they carry their own
# guards instead (CONFIRM_DATABASE, I_HAVE_A_BACKUP, a typed confirmation).
# Not distributing them means a fresh clone cannot run either one by accident,
# and neither shows up in a diff for someone to copy the pattern from.
#
# The trade: git is not backing these up. If you need them on another machine,
# copy them across deliberately rather than expecting a clone to carry them.
scripts/reset-production-data.ts
scripts/create-admin.ts

# Database dumps taken before a reset — these hold real customer data.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
